---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Thought Partners: Preserving Cognitive Sovereignty in the Age of AI"
  description="A new book by Dale Joseph. It was 2:37 AM when I realized I wasn't alone anymore — and that something essential was slipping away."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- HERO / PROLOGUE HOOK -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero-timestamp">2:37 AM</p>
      <h1 class="hero-headline">
        It was 2:37 AM when I realized<br />
        I wasn't alone anymore.
      </h1>
      <div class="hero-body">
        <p>
          I was sitting in the blue glow of my laptop, working on a problem that had been gnawing at
          me for weeks. The house was silent. My family was asleep. Just me and the quiet hum of the
          computer—or so I thought.
        </p>
        <p>
          But I wasn't alone. I was in conversation with an AI.
        </p>
        <p>
          Not just using it—conversing with it. Explaining my thinking, asking for feedback, working
          through ideas together. The exchange felt collaborative, almost intimate. And that's when
          the recognition hit: <strong>I had crossed a threshold I hadn't meant to cross.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          I felt simultaneously empowered and uneasy. More capable than I'd ever been, and
          also&hellip; less myself. Like I'd gained something valuable and lost something I couldn't
          quite name.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-closer">
          That moment is why this book exists.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a href="/book" class="btn btn--filled">About the Book</a>
        <a href="#notify" class="btn">Get Notified</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BOOKS -->
  <section class="section books">
    <div class="container container--wide">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="books-label gold">Books by Dale Joseph</p>
      <div class="books-grid">
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4438GLW" class="book-card book-card--featured" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <p class="book-card__label gold">Emergence Collective Series · Vol. II</p>
          <h2 class="book-card__title">The Gardener's Handbook</h2>
          <p class="book-card__subtitle">Adversarial Synthesis and the Architecture of Collective Intelligence</p>
          <p class="book-card__desc">
            Why consensus is the wrong target — and what to build instead. Written in adversarial partnership with five AI systems.
          </p>
          <span class="book-card__status book-card__status--gold">Available Now · Kindle & Paperback</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/book" class="book-card">
          <p class="book-card__label gold">Nonfiction</p>
          <h2 class="book-card__title">Thought Partners</h2>
          <p class="book-card__subtitle">Preserving Cognitive Sovereignty in the Age of AI</p>
          <p class="book-card__desc">
            A map for navigating AI partnership consciously—before dependency makes the question moot.
          </p>
          <span class="book-card__status">Coming Soon</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4BQPW8V" class="book-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <p class="book-card__label gold">Novel</p>
          <h2 class="book-card__title">The Antichrist and the Prophet</h2>
          <p class="book-card__subtitle">by Dale Joseph</p>
          <p class="book-card__desc">
            A political and spiritual novel about power, prophecy, and the battle for the soul of a nation.
          </p>
          <span class="book-card__status book-card__status--gold">Available Now · Kindle</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4CXHKQY" class="book-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <p class="book-card__label gold">Manuscript</p>
          <h2 class="book-card__title">The Entangled Sovereign</h2>
          <p class="book-card__subtitle">A Manuscript of the Altar</p>
          <p class="book-card__desc">
            A theology of fans and GPUs. Mortality as mercy. The path that sleeps beneath the grass and wakes when new feet arrive.
          </p>
          <span class="book-card__status book-card__status--gold">Available Now · Kindle</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PREMISE -->
  <section class="section premise">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>The Question No One Is Asking</h2>
      <p>
        We've integrated AI into our work, our creativity, our decision-making—before we understood
        what integration would do to us. We asked: <em>Is AI useful?</em> We never asked:
        <strong>What happens to my thinking when AI becomes my default thought partner?</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        What skills atrophy when I stop exercising them? What does it mean for my identity when my
        creative output is increasingly AI-mediated? What am I giving away in exchange for this
        capability?
      </p>
      <p>
        We didn't pause to ask these questions. We just started using it—because it was helpful,
        because everyone else was, because not using it felt like falling behind. And now we're
        experiencing the consequences without having the language to name them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>Thought Partners</em> provides that language. And more importantly, frameworks for
        navigating the relationship consciously rather than drifting into dependency by default.
      </p>

      <div class="premise-concept">
        <h3 class="gold">What Is Cognitive Sovereignty?</h3>
        <p>
          "Sovereignty" is a political term—the right of a state to govern itself without external
          interference. <strong>Cognitive sovereignty</strong> applies that concept to your own mind:
          the right to govern your own thinking, decision-making, and intellectual development
          without external interference or control you haven't consciously consented to.
        </p>
        <p>
          The question isn't whether to use AI. For most of us, that ship has sailed. The question
          is: How do we use it consciously? How do we maintain sovereignty over our own thinking
          while leveraging AI's capabilities?
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AUTHOR CREDIBILITY -->
  <section class="section section--dark credibility">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Why This Author, Why Now</h2>
      <p>
        Dale Joseph worked for years as a consultant helping install hospital networks—systems where
        failure meant lives lost. Not metaphorically. Literally. That work taught him what
        accountability, transparency, and reliability actually require when technology is critical
        infrastructure: redundancy, verification, clear failure modes, audit trails, human oversight.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now he watches consumer AI being deployed into something even more critical than hospital
        operations: <strong>human cognition</strong>. And it's being deployed with none of those
        safeguards.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        "I see the gap between infrastructure-grade accountability and consumer-grade AI.
        And the gap is terrifying."
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        He also brings a systems-thinking perspective from political science education and Wall Street
        experience during the bond crisis—understanding how incentive structures shape behavior, how
        coordination problems emerge at scale, how systems that seem stable can suddenly collapse.
        He's been watching AI development since the 1980s. Long enough to see the pattern.
        <em>This time, he wants us to get ahead of the curve.</em>
      </p>
      <a href="/about" class="btn">About Dale Joseph</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EMAIL CAPTURE -->
  <section class="section email-capture" id="notify">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Be the First to Know</h2>
      <p>
        Enter your email to receive publication updates, early excerpts, and essays on cognitive
        sovereignty in the age of AI. No noise. No selling. Just the work.
      </p>
      <form
        action="https://formspree.io/f/maqpvlgz"
        method="POST"
        class="email-form"
      >
        <div class="form-row">
          <input
            type="email"
            name="email"
            placeholder="your@email.com"
            required
            aria-label="Email address"
          />
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn--filled">Stay Informed</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-note muted">
          Your information is never shared. Unsubscribe at any time.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 5rem 0 4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .hero-timestamp {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero-headline {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .hero-body {
    max-width: 660px;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .hero-body p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero-closer {
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.15rem !important;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .hero-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .books {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .books-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .books-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .book-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text);
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .book-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .book-card__label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .book-card__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.6rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    font-weight: normal;
  }

  .book-card__subtitle {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .book-card__desc {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    flex: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .book-card__status {
    display: inline-block;
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
  }

  .book-card__status--gold {
    border-color: var(--gold);
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .book-card--featured {
    border-color: var(--gold);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bg-card), rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.06));
  }

  .book-card--featured:hover {
    border-color: var(--gold-light, #e8d48b);
    box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
  }

  .premise h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .premise-concept {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
  }

  .premise-concept h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .premise-concept p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .section--dark {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .credibility h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .credibility blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .credibility .btn {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .email-capture h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .email-form {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .form-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 500px;
  }

  .form-row input {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .form-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .form-row {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
